Z||000000||GTDusty||12-21-2001||06:08 PM|||| Ok I need a little help to have my fiero running by christmas. My car wont charge for some reason..I already replaced the battery and had the alternator checked. The napa guy said it was probably a fusable link. I traced down the alt. wires to just behind the battery but found 4 fusable links! How do I know which one is bad? Also I noticed that the little clip that plugs into the top of the alternator...that wire is spliced into the big wire on the back of the alternator a little ways down. You know what Im saying right? Could that be the problem.? Someone lemme know!!<P> Dusty||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||12-21-2001||09:34 PM||||To check it, remove the negative batt cable and check continuity from the alt terminal and up at the junction block.  If it is shot you definitely need to replace it.  If it is not open, you may still need to replace it because it can limit current but not burn.  So this test is a positive failure test if it is open.  If you can get your hands on an ammeter to put inline that will tell you what is able to flow through the fuse. GL||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-22-2001||12:10 PM||||The patched in wire is an indication of a previous problem......prob with the fuseable link.  See if you have 12v on the big wire and with the car running you should have fire on both of the small wires.  If not...it can't charge.  If the big wire doesn't have fire on it all the time then you're just gonna have to trace it down and find the burned fuseable link.....prob near the starter.  Good Luck<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
